00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:51.000
upon by other agencies to provide support as required. In early June of 1992, the ATF received one request from a sheriff's department in Texas who said that they were dealing with a situation in McLennan County near the city of Waco. It had all started with some reports of troubling things being sent in the mail. Larry Gilbreath was a driver for the United Parcel Service, or U.S. and he had been delivering parcels to the Mount Carmel compound since 1986. Sometimes he made several deliveries in one week. Initially, he'd thought nothing of it.

